-- title:
--   Local equality of ideals gives an idempotent generator modulo I
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a commutative noetherian ring and let $I \subseteq J$ be ideals of $P$. Assume that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $P$ with $J \subseteq \mathfrak n$, the ideals generated by the images of $J$ and of $I$ in the localisation $P_{\mathfrak n}$ coincide, i.e. $\mathrm{Ideal.map}$ of $J$ along the structure map $P \to \mathrm{Localization.AtPrime}\ \mathfrak n$ equals that of $I$. The conclusion is that there exists an element $e$ of the quotient ring $P/I$ which is idempotent, $e^2 = e$, such that the image ideal $\mathrm{Ideal.map}\ (\mathrm{Ideal.Quotient.mk}\ I)\ J$ — that is, the ideal $J/I$ of $P/I$ — is the principal ideal $\mathrm{Ideal.span}\ \{e\}$. Note that the localisation hypothesis is imposed only at maximal ideals containing $J$, and that the conclusion asserts idempotency of the ring element $e$ together with the equality $J/I = (e)$, not merely that the ideal $J/I$ is idempotent.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of the statement that an ideal which vanishes locally at every maximal ideal of its support-complement and is otherwise the unit ideal cuts out a clopen subset of the spectrum, hence is generated by an idempotent; here $J/I \subseteq P/I$ is locally $0$ at the maximal ideals containing $J$ and locally the unit ideal elsewhere. It is used in the construction of square presentations of $p$-divisible groups over rings of integers, where it removes the discrepancy between the ideal of a presentation and the square ideal produced beforehand, via [`PDivisibleGroup.exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.exists_square_presentation_level_of_ringOfIntegers).
